# Input

Keyboard, mouse, up to 4 connected gamepads and 10 pointer touches are sampled once per rendered simulation frame, shared by Update/FixedUpdate/LateUpdate. GetKeyDown/GetButtonDown describe that frame, not one individual callback. Keyboard input is accepted from Game (main or detached); typing in editors is excluded. Mouse position/touch pixels use the active Game canvas backing resolution with bottom-left origin; mouse scroll is browser wheel units. Gamepad axes use a configurable dead zone; browser permissions and a physical controller interaction may be required before devices appear.

GetButton supports Jump (Space/pad A), Fire1 (left mouse/right trigger), Submit, Cancel. RebindButton and RebindAxis are Axiom extensions with browser KeyboardEvent.code controls (KeyE, Enter, Mouse0, Gamepad0/Button1). SaveBindingOverridesAsJson / LoadBindingOverridesFromJson serialize only overrides; save explicitly with PlayerPrefs. No Unity Input System package, interactive binding dialog, haptics, gyroscope, pen or OS-global input is claimed. GetAxis is raw, without legacy axis smoothing.

```csharp
public override void Start() { Input.RebindButton("Interact", "KeyE", "Gamepad0/Button1"); }
public override void Update() {
 if (Input.GetButtonDown("Interact")) Debug.Log("Interact");
 transform.position += Vector3.right * Input.GetAxisRaw("Horizontal") * Time.deltaTime;
}
```

See Touch and KeyCode. Input & Persistence API Lab exercises saved overrides and per-project score.

